  clock: 3  # 503f
  nonce: 503f  # 503f
  message: "EVIDENCE 2026-09-23 (IoPrimitive.kind concept audit, INV-zikab; write-up §6 S5). THE SWIFT MEMBERS OF THIS FAMILY HAVE NEVER FIRED, AND THE KIND IS WHY. swift.yaml keys 16 constructor rows as `methods:` (URLRequest, HTTPClientRequest, NWConnection, NWListener, Logger, ServerBootstrap, ClientBootstrap, MultiThreadedEventLoopGroup, NIOSSLCertificate/Context/PrivateKey, NIOAsyncChannel, NIOWebSocketServerUpgrader, NSFetchRequest, ModelContext, CommandLine). The analyzer emits `URLRequest(url:)` as swift:external:0-0:URLRequest (no stamp, hint `external`), so gate_named_entry drops every method row: zero matches.\nRe-kinding them to function would ACTIVATE 115 edges on 4 repos (vapor +26, hummingbird +76, SwiftLint +1, Alamofire +12). All 14 sampled are genuine calls of the named constructor. BUT MOST OF THE BOUNDARIES ARE WRONG, and nothing ever exercised them:\n  - Logger(label:) rowed logging (41 on hummingbird) only builds a logger.\n  - MultiThreadedEventLoopGroup rowed net_recv is a thread pool.\n  - NIOSSLPrivateKey(file:) and NIOSSLCertificate(file:) rowed net_send READ A FILE (fs_read).\n  - URLRequest and HTTPClientRequest rowed net_send build a value.\n  - CommandLine is a static property (CommandLine.arguments), never called.\nSo a mis-keyed kind has hidden mis-keyed boundaries. Adjudicate each row (delete / re-boundary / re-kind) before any kind change. A blind re-kind turns a recall gap into false positives."  # 503f
- op: discuss  # 5ae4
  at: '2026-09-23T21:14:38Z'  # 5ae4
  by: agent  # 5ae4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5ae4
  clock: 4  # 5ae4
  nonce: 5ae4  # 5ae4
  message: "SWIFT SLICE DONE, PR #1158 (2026-09-23; INV-zikab step 3). Each of the 16 swift constructor rows was decided against ADR-0049 ruling 1, then keyed function (ADR-0059).\n- DELETED (the constructor crosses nothing): URLRequest, HTTPClientRequest, ClientBootstrap, MultiThreadedEventLoopGroup, Logger's constructor, NIOSSLContext/Certificate/PrivateKey. The NIOSSL (file:) forms read a file, but the label is not on the edge, and 17 of 22 uses in vapor + hummingbird are (bytes:).\n- DISCLOSED (ADR-0049 ruling 3; the boundary is in place and the rows had never fired): NWListener, ServerBootstrap, NIOWebSocketServerUpgrader -> net_listen; NSFetchRequest -> db_compose.\n- HANDLE, boundary kept (ADR-0049 holds the handle shape in every language): NWConnection net_send, NIOAsyncChannel net_recv, ModelContext db_read.\n- CommandLine -> attributes: [arguments] env_read. It is unreachable: swift emits no module_attr_ref.\nMEASURED on 6 swift surveys: vapor 66->69 and hummingbird 88->90 classified; the other 4 unchanged; coverage gate and untyped disclosures unchanged. verify-claims A/B on vapor + hummingbird: 14/14 verdicts identical (all were already inconclusive on coverage).\nTHIS ITEM STAYS violated. Its FILED rows (python urllib.request.Request, go net/http.NewRequest, erlang/elixir ets.new, elixir Req.new) are untouched; the swift members were evidence added later.\nRESIDUAL, not filed separately: the real swift I/O these constructors stood in for is unrowed (NWConnection start/send/receive, ServerBootstrap.bind, ClientBootstrap.connect, HTTPClient.execute, NIOSSLCertificate.fromPEMFile, ModelContext fetch/save). The objc ledger rows NSMutableURLRequest.requestWithURL: and NSFetchRequest.fetchRequestWithEntityName: have the same shapes, a request value and a lazy query; WI-ziviv must decide their boundaries before re-kinding them."  # 5ae4
