  clock: 6  # 7a89
  nonce: 7a89  # 7a89
  message: "PARTIAL, PR #1173 (merged 2026-09-24). THIS ITEM STAYS VIOLATED: two of its five filed rows remain, each blocked by a filed prerequisite.\n\nLOADED ROWS ON MERGED DEV 9caa8c8c94:\n  python  urllib.request.Request  net_send   KEPT, blocked by WI-bakik\n  go      net/http.NewRequest     net_send   KEPT, blocked by WI-jikik\n  erlang  ets.new                 (none)     REMOVED\n  elixir  ets.new                 (none)     REMOVED (inherited from erlang)\n  elixir  Req.new                 (none)     REMOVED (overlay)\n  elixir  Finch.build             (none)     REMOVED (overlay; same shape, found in the family sweep)\n  elixir  Req.Request.run_request net_send   ADDED, the executor plausible uses\n\nTHE PRE-REGISTERED QUESTION (\"does the flow survive the row going away?\"), answered per language on fixtures (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/gujoh_09242026/FX_AB.txt):\n- python: YES. As a plain call it becomes ddg-confirmed at urlopen.\n- erlang, elixir: YES, at ets.insert, Req.request! and Finch.request.\n- go: YES with a typed client. NO through http.DefaultClient.Do: violated -> inconclusive, because the package variable is untyped.\n\nFINDING-LEVEL COHORT A/B, generic taint claims, pinned worktrees (VC_AB.txt):\n- 9 repos: rebar3, cowboy, ejabberd, vernemq, plausible, beads, harbor, livebook, mlflow.\n- 0 verdicts moved.\n- Every function that lost constructor evidence gained it at its executor, with two exceptions:\n  * plausible: `Req.new() |> Req.Request.run_request()` had no rowed executor, so the executor was rowed in the same change.\n  * livebook: build_req is a zero-argument `Req.new()`, a false attribution.\n\nWHY PYTHON IS KEPT: this is a gate effect, not a finding effect. Without the row, `Request(...)` is an unclassified call into an unenumerated module, and _uncatalogued_external_modules withholds the clean verdict, per-module by design (INV-buzab). scripts/check-self-claims --minimal moved all 18 self-claims to inconclusive, because hypergumbo_tracker/stop_hook.py builds a Request. The same run on dev is clean. `stdlib_other` does not lift that gate (probed). The row now carries a note saying why it stays.\n\nALSO FILED: WI-hular (P3), no confirmed DDG walk into a `with` item. It is the same in both arms.\n\nThe ets.new removal also carries the gate effect in principle. The erlang fixture's network claim went confirmed -> inconclusive, but on the 6 BEAM repos nothing moved, because they were already violated or inconclusive. Disclosed in the commit."  # 7a89
